    "note": "ATD is zero-shot (no training, no model). LOSO is equivalent to the full-set evaluation because each speaker's ATD is computed against reference embeddings from disjoint control speakers. Note that the ATD scale (mean reference-distance) is not in the {0,1,2} severity space, so RMSE/MAE are scale-mismatched and meaningful only for rho/rank-accuracy comparison."
  },
  "method_notes": "Frozen WavLM-Large; utterance feature = mean-pool of transformer layer 9 (1024-d). Regression head trained per-fold under leave-one-speaker-out across the 15 TORGO speakers. For each LOSO fold, hyperparameters were tuned by 5-fold group-CV on the 14 training speakers (Ridge alpha in {0.1,1,10,100,1000}; LinearSVR C in {0.01,0.1,1,10}). Per-utterance severity predictions were averaged to a single speaker-level prediction; metrics are reported on the n=15 speaker-level predictions. This frozen-backbone + classifier-head reproduction follows Hernandez et al. (2020) and Schu et al. (2023) in spirit; full backbone fine-tuning is degenerate at n=15 speakers. ATD is included for apples-to-apples comparison and is zero-shot (no training), so its LOSO and full-set metrics are equivalent.",
  "config": {
    "backbone": "microsoft/wavlm-large (frozen)",
    "feature_layer": 9,
    "pooling": "mean over time",
    "ssl_regression_heads": [
      "sklearn.linear_model.Ridge",
      "sklearn.svm.LinearSVR (squared_epsilon_insensitive)"
    ],
    "mfcc_baseline": "58-d MFCC/acoustic features (src.baselines.extract_mfcc_features) + RBF SVR; C in {0.1,1,10,100}, gamma in {scale,1e-3,1e-2,1e-1} selected by nested GroupKFold CV per LOSO fold",
    "cv_for_hp": "<=5-fold GroupKFold by speaker on the training fold; StandardScaler fit on inner-train split only (nested)",
    "loso_speakers": [
